WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Initial observation
A frozen causal VAE encodes the video; the first temporal latent slice retains the initial observation.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Render and action encoding
Camera-aligned robot renderings and numerical joint and gripper trajectories provide conditioning.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Render–action fusion
Render tokens supply the queries; action tokens supply the keys and values in cross-attention.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Per-token timestep modulation
Each video token receives a conditioning vector added to its flow-timestep embedding.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Future video prediction
The video backbone predicts future frames from the initial observation and robot conditioning.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Shared trainable parameters
The adapter and backbone are trained jointly across embodiments; the VAE and robot renderers stay fixed.
